        {
          "question": "How can I keep the same face across all six portraits?",
          "answer": "Use the same clear, permitted adult reference image and keep the core identity instructions stable. A reference can guide facial characteristics but cannot guarantee an exact match."
        },
        {
          "question": "How can I preserve detail in a black suit?",
          "answer": "Request visible fabric texture, lapel edges, seams, buttons, folds, and controlled highlights so the tailoring does not merge into featureless shadows."
        },
        {
          "question": "How can I prevent a white suit from looking overexposed?",
          "answer": "Ask for visible fabric texture, seams, folds, tonal separation, and preserved highlights, then review the output for clipped white areas."
        },
        {
          "question": "How can I improve hands and mirror reflections?",
          "answer": "Simplify hand actions and explicitly request identical identity, clothing, hairstyle, and accessories in the reflection. Remove extra mirrors if consistency problems continue."
        }
